From 7ca0afc1d4da5c0207fa94388aa0718d86eceec8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gonzoblasco <15630819+gonzoblasco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:50:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: resolve hidden input anchor via CSS custom property

Replaces the layout effect and per-render getComputedStyle with a custom
property, and switches to `inset` for the anchor offsets.

- Point both the component's outer element and the hidden input at the
  same custom property, so a consumer name declared in a class name or
  an ancestor is adopted; previously an inline default masked it
- Replace the layout effect and getComputedStyle with the custom property,
  so the anchor name resolves in the cascade instead of on re-render
- Use the inset shorthand instead of top/left plus anchor-size, which
  sizes the content box: the input's border and padding made it 8x6px
  larger than the component, and it is correct in RTL
- Use useId from react-aria/useId instead of Math.random, which broke
  SSR, and drop the anchor ref merge
- Remove the per-component screen reader focus ring stories; the behavior
  is on by default and the browser tests cover it
- Add RTL, per-instance anchor, and custom property browser tests
